course: dictionary
lesson: 10025
title: Tenner: slang for ten pounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tenner is informal slang, used in chatty talk, for a ten-pound note or for ten pounds. In the UK you may also hear it for ten euros or ten dollars. «It cost me a tenner.» The word "cost" tells you this is about money, so a tenner means ten pounds.
explain: Look at the words around the word to choose its meaning. «I gave Sam two tenners for the tickets.» Two tenners means twenty, because each tenner is ten. Quick check: swap in "ten pounds" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Tenner can also mean the number ten in some games or prizes. If the sentence talks about cost, pay or pounds, it means money. If it talks about a game, a score or a prize number, it may mean ten.
fact: Tenner is informal slang, so you hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
fact: A tenner is ten pounds, ten euros or ten dollars, or a banknote worth ten.
fact: «Two tenners» means twenty.
fact: Related money slang: a fiver is five, a quid is one pound, and a grand is a thousand.
fact: In some games or prizes, tenner can mean the number ten.
exercise: «It cost me a tenner.» What does a tenner mean here? | *Ten pounds | A tennis racket | A hundred pounds | Five pounds
exercise: «I gave Sam two tenners for the tickets.» How much money did I give him? | 2 pounds | 12 pounds | *20 pounds | 100 pounds
exercise: Mia says, «A fiver is five pounds.» What is a quid? | Ten pounds | *One pound | One thousand pounds | Five pounds
test: Jayden's mum says, «Let's split the bill: a tenner each.» How much does each person pay? | Twenty pounds | One pound | Five pounds | *Ten pounds
test: Ella says she won a tenner on the prize wheel, and the prize is the number ten. What does tenner mean in this game? | A slice of cake | *The number ten | A type of bird | A lost sock
exam: Which informal word means ten pounds? | grand | *tenner | quid | fiver
